From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrii Sultanov <andriy.sultanov@vates.tech>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 13:07:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add support for ARM domains

Introduce `arm` as a new VM domain type, so that ARM guests can be
created and started. For now, only direct boot is supported.

xapi:
- Add `arm` to the domain_type enum and update the known schema hash.
  The copy of domain_type_to_string in the record_util tests gains the
  arm case.
- Handle `arm in the domain type matches, mostly like PVH. Unlike PVH,
  the host isn't checked for HVM support, and HA failover plans with the
  dynamic min memory. Indirect boot is rejected.
- Account memory for ARM VMs with the new ARM memory model and a fixed
  shadow multiplier of 1.0, matching what xenopsd allocates.
- Skip CPU featureset levelling for ARM. VMs return an empty featureset
  and skip the vendor/feature compatibility check, as there is no CPU
  policy for ARM yet.

xenopsd:
- Add the Vm.ARM type and a BuildARM builder carrying the kernel cmdline
  and boot modules. A ramdisk configured via PV-ramdisk is passed to
  xenguest as a boot module.
- Add an ARM memory model. Its "shadow" allocation is the P2M pool,
  sized like libxl does on ARM. So, 256 pages per vCPU, 1 page per MiB
  of RAM, and 128 pages for the extended regions, rounded up to whole
  MiB.
- On ARM, set and read the P2M pool size via
  paging_mempool_size_{set,get} instead of shadow_allocation_{set,get},
  as XEN_DOMCTL_SHADOW_OP_{GET,SET}_ALLOCATION are x86-only. This covers
  build_pre, the shadow correction after the build, the memory
  breakdown, list_domains and squeezed. Changing the shadow multiplier
  of an ARM domain is refused.
- Build ARM domains like PVH guests, with build_pre and xenguest in
  pvh_build mode, but with the ARM memory model.
- Write domain-type "arm-pvh" and treat ARM guests as always enlightened
  when waiting for a shutdown acknowledgement.
- Refuse suspend, resume and restore of ARM domains with Unimplemented.
  Importing the metadata of an ARM VM isn't supported either.
- Request a vGIC version based on the GICv2/GICv3 support reported by
  the host's physinfo, preferring GICv3 like libxl. ARM guests get no
  SPIs, as there is no vPL011, virtio-mmio or passthrough.

Signed-off-by: Andrii Sultanov <andriy.sultanov@vates.tech>
Signed-off-by: Julian Vetter <julian.vetter@vates.tech>

